-- ── Verification is not seed data ──────────────────────────────────────────
-- These rows used to ship verification_status = 'verified', a trust_score,
-- and a verification_nodes array of per-check results -- "Title: pass",
-- "Survey: pass", "Flood: pending" -- all of it generated. No one looked at
-- any of these properties, because none of them exists.
--
-- On a demo that is a nice screenshot. On a live database it is 120 homes
-- telling buyers that Synapse checked their title, and the platform has a
-- trigger (properties_guard_verification) specifically to stop anyone
-- setting these fields casually. A seed file should not be the way round it.
--
-- They now seed as unverified with no score and no check nodes, which is
-- what an unchecked listing actually is. Verification arrives through the
-- verification desk, on real documents, or it does not arrive.
--
-- Safe for Tayo: toju-chat ranks on verification rather than filtering on
-- it, so unverified homes are still recommended -- labelled -- and Tayo says
-- which is which.
on conflict (id) do nothing;
